  "details": "1. Open a VRChat Unity Project with the latest VRC supported Unity Version (atm 2022.3.22f1).\n\n2. Build and *Publish* the world.\n\n3. Visit the published world.\n\n4. Press `Shift + Back Quote + 2`.\n\n5. Take note of the world version reported (after `W:`).\n\n6. Back in the Unity Editor, Build & Test the world with 1 client.\n\n7. Press `Shift + Back Quote + 2` in the test client.\n\n8. Notice the world version states the client version instead of matching the stated version of the world (after `V:`).\n\nFor example, using VRC Quick Launcher, I can launch a build from the year 2023 and it will report Unity 6, which is not true.",
